<font size="+1">

<p>
The research group on Computing and Data Understanding at eXtreme Scale (CDUX)
pursues problems in scientific visualization, high-performance computing,
scientific computing, information visualization, and computer graphics, 
and especially focuses on problems where these areas intersect.
We perform research for 
the <a href="http://energy.gov">Department of Energy</a>, 
for the <a href="http://nsf.gov">National Science Foundation</a>,
and for private industry.
This research is delivered in widely used software tools, like
<a href="http://www.llnl.gov/visit">VisIt</a>, and helps develop new
tools, 
like <a href="http://m.vtk.org/index.php/Main_Page">VTK-m</a>, a visualization library for many-core architectures,
and like <a href="https://www.tacc.utexas.edu/research-development/tacc-software/gravit">GraviT</a>, a distributed-memory parallel ray-tracing library.
The results of our research are often published at premier venues,
like the <a href="http://ieeevis.org">IEEE 
Visualization</a> 
and <a href="http://supercomputing.org">ACM/IEEE SuperComputing (SC)</a> conferences.
</p>
<p>
CDUX is part of the <a href="http://cs.uoregon.edu/">Computer and Information
Science Department</a> at the <a href="http://uoregon.edu">University of 
Oregon</a>.
</p>


